## 8. Password Reset Flow Architecture & Prople Store UI Enforcement

### Root Cause Analysis of Missing OTP and Default Firebase UI
1. **The Issue**:
   - When users requested a password reset, `sendPasswordResetEmail(auth, cleanEmail)` was called prior to the custom API endpoint.
   - This triggered Firebase's default email template from `noreply@prople-store-3efed.firebaseapp.com`, which contains no OTP code and links to Google's default barebones webpage (`prople-store-3efed.firebaseapp.com/__/auth/action?mode=resetPassword&oobCode=...`).
   - Clicking this link bypassed the Prople Store application interface entirely and presented a generic white/blue form.

2. **The High-Fidelity Prople Store Reset Architecture**:
   - **Exclusive Custom Mail Dispatch**: Client invokes `/api/auth/forgot-password` exclusively, eliminating plain automated Firebase mail triggers.
   - **Customized Recipient & Names**: `formatRecipientName()` dynamically title-cases and personalizes the user's name from account metadata.
   - **All-in-One Email Layout**: The single custom email delivers:
     - The official Prople Store logo and GitHub dark-mode container.
     - A cryptographically secure 6-digit OTP code (`code`) in 34px bold letter-spaced typography.
     - The direct action button (`Reset Password Directly →`) linking to `https://www.prople.co.in/?auth=reset-password&email=...&code=...`.
   - **Clean Authentication UI**:
     - No external link buttons appear on the authentication screen; users only see the clean 6-digit verification code input.
     - If the user prefers clicking the button directly in their email, it auto-fills and verifies the code on Prople Store.
   - **Universal UI Catchment**:
     - `AuthPage.tsx` and `NavigationContext.tsx` intercept incoming reset routes (`?auth=reset-password`, `?action=reset-password`, `?mode=reset-password`, `?mode=resetPassword`, and `?oobCode=...`) and display the native Prople Store password form.

